    "summary": "Cross-client response injection and disclosure in self-hosted Next.js applications forwarding fetched responses",
    "description": "<!-- https://linear.app/vercel/issue/NSEC-564 -->\r\nSelf-hosted Next.js applications (App Router route handlers and the fetch cache) that return a fetched upstream response unchanged can emit a response whose declared framing does not match the body actually sent. When such an application sits behind an HTTP/1.1 reverse proxy that permits pipelined response queueing, a crafted upstream response can desynchronize responses between clients, enabling response injection and disclosure of other clients' responses.",
